From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: sensor: Add properties for IMX320 and IMX345

Neither sensor is in the properties database, so libcamera warns that it is
"assuming unverified defaults" and uses a gain delay of one frame. Every
other Sony sensor in the database except the imx219 and imx283 applies gain
two frames later, and assuming one frame makes the AGC correct against a
frame that has not taken the previous correction yet -- the loop then
overshoots on a scene change and clips.

Pixel pitches are from the Galaxy S9, which pairs a 1.4um rear IMX345 with a
1.22um front IMX320. The delays follow the Sony family convention rather than
individual measurement.

--- a/b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -256,10 +256,30 @@
 			.testPatternModes = {},
 			.sensorDelays = { },
 		} },
+		{ "imx320", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 1220, 1220 },
+			.testPatternModes = {},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
+		} },
 		{ "imx335", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 2000, 2000 },
 			.testPatternModes = {},
 			.sensorDelays = { },
+		} },
+		{ "imx345", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 1400, 1400 },
+			.testPatternModes = {},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
 		} },
 		{ "imx415", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1450, 1450 },
